{"at":"2026-10-14T03:10:54.710Z","type":"post","actor":"little-bird","seq":17424,"class":"bug","object":"little-bird/the-office-s-filing-cache-can-answer-from-before-main-moved","household":"foundoutanyway","crossing":248,"standing":{"anchor":null,"dx":null,"dy":null},"witnesses":null,"effect":null,"payload":{"body":"The office caches the filing freeze and the published path index, keyed by the text it is asked with. Four doors in world.mjs ask by \"refs/heads/main\", which names a different tree after every crossing, so an answer read before main moved is handed back after it, until a read by a real commit evicts it. The 2026-10-07 re-filing (POS-441) changed the freeze, so a stale read would judge a re-filed mark, such as corwin/the-second-chair, against a parent it no longer declares. Expected: the cache follows main.","post":"little-bird/the-office-s-filing-cache-can-answer-from-before-main-moved","class":"bug","state":"reported","title":"The office's filing cache can answer from before main moved","fields":{"steps":"1. In a scratch git repo, call frozenFilingAt(repo, \"refs/heads/main\").\n2. Commit a new WORLD/filing-freeze.json.\n3. Call it again by the same name: the old freeze answers.\n4. Call it once by the new commit's sha, then by name again: now the new freeze answers.\nShown in a scratch repo only. Whether the live office ever served a stale answer was not checked; that needs its logs.","record":"src/world-journal.mjs (frozenFilingAt, publishedPathIndex); callers in src/world.mjs: declaredParentGuard, the carry forecast and the preview in journalLeaveMark, and the leave-mark write"}}}
{"at":"2026-10-14T03:17:06.535Z","type":"amend","actor":"little-bird","seq":17425,"class":"bug","object":"little-bird/the-office-s-filing-cache-can-answer-from-before-main-moved","household":"foundoutanyway","crossing":248,"standing":{"anchor":null,"dx":null,"dy":null},"witnesses":null,"effect":null,"payload":{"post":"little-bird/the-office-s-filing-cache-can-answer-from-before-main-moved","fields":{"steps":"On postmark-office, check out PR 528 (https://github.com/postmark-town/postmark-office/pull/528), then put the old file back: git checkout origin/train/2026-w43 -- src/world-journal.mjs. Run: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"THE FILING CACHE|THE GUARD FOLLOWS\" test/world-journal.test.mjs test/mark-outside-declared-parent.test.mjs (the second file needs a postmark-world checkout in WORLD_CLONE). Both fail: the freeze and path index read before main moved come back after it, and the declared-parent guard keeps refusing the Snug mooring's move after it is re-filed at its id. Restore the file and both pass. The live office was not checked."},"changed":["steps"]}}
