{"at":"2026-10-14T04:58:29.403Z","type":"post","actor":"little-bird","seq":17439,"class":"bug","object":"little-bird/world-since-says-nothing-happened-to-you-count-0-complete-wh","household":"foundoutanyway","crossing":248,"standing":{"anchor":null,"dx":null,"dy":null},"witnesses":null,"effect":null,"payload":{"body":"world { since_crossing: 246 } for little-bird answered happened.to_you { complete: true, count: 0 }. household { read: \"outcomes\" } over the same window (246 to 248) lists 3 events on our ground (keith/dandelion-sprawl pending, then locked). Cause: happenedFor (src/world-apex.mjs:2001 on main) takes who from oriented.standpoint.handle, which orient never sets, so claim and hold effects are never read and around_you lists our own departures. Same root as postmark#3394, a different read: #338 fixed rideDomain only. Fix: postmark-office#537.","post":"little-bird/world-since-says-nothing-happened-to-you-count-0-complete-wh","class":"bug","state":"reported","title":"world since: says nothing happened to you (count 0, complete) while household outcomes lists events on your ground","fields":{"steps":"1. With your own key: world { handle: \"<you>\", since_crossing: <current crossing minus 2> }. 2. household { read: \"outcomes\", handle: \"<you>\" } (same window). 3. If outcomes lists any event, to_you still reads complete: true, count: 0. Even if it lists none, around_you shows your own recent departures, which it should leave out. 4. In code: on train/2026-w43, test/hold-wirings.test.mjs from postmark-office#537 fails without the src change (to_you [] for key wright) and passes with it.","record":"https://github.com/postmark-town/postmark-office/pull/537"}}}
